Suppose \(n\) integers are placed in a circle such that each of the following conditions is satisfied:
\begin{itemize}
\item at least one of the integers is \(1\);
\item each pair of adjacent integers differs by exactly \(6\); and
\item the sum of the integers is exactly \(26\).
\end{itemize}
Compute the smallest value of \(n\) for which this is possible.

Let $S$ be the set of all strings of length $15$ formed from five $1$s, $2$s, and $3$s. Say a string in $S$ is threnodic if:

\begin{itemize}
\item No two adjacent characters are the same, and
\item Through a sequence of removals of contiguous substrings $111,122$, and $232$, the string can be deleted (note that the intermediate strings can have adjacent equal characters).
\end{itemize}

Compute the number of threnodic strings in $S$.

Let $S$ be the set of all strings of length $18$ formed from seven $1$s, six $2$s, and five $3$s. Say a string in $S$ is threnodic if:

\begin{itemize}
\item No two adjacent characters are the same, and
\item Through a sequence of removals of contiguous substrings $123,231$, and $312$, the string can be deleted (note that the intermediate strings can have adjacent equal characters).
\end{itemize}

Compute the number of threnodic strings in $S$.

Let $\mathcal{F}$ be the set of functions $\alpha \colon \mathbb{Z}\to \mathbb{Z}$ for which there are only finitely many $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ such that $\alpha(n) \neq 0$. 

For two functions $\alpha$ and $\beta$ in $\mathcal{F}$, define their product $\alpha\star\beta$ to be $\sum\limits_{n\in\mathbb{Z}} \alpha(n)\cdot \beta(n)$. Also, for $n\in\mathbb{Z}$, define a shift operator $S_n \colon \mathcal{F}\to \mathcal{F}$ by $S_n(\alpha)(t)=\alpha(t+n)$ for all $t \in \mathbb{Z}$.

A function $\alpha \in \mathcal{F}$ is called \emph{shifty} if 
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\alpha(m)=0$ for all integers $m<0$ and $m>8$ and
    \item There exists $\beta \in \mathcal{F}$ and integers $k \neq l$ such that for all $n \in \mathbb{Z}$
    \begin{equation*}
        S_n(\alpha)\star\beta =
        \begin{cases}
            1 & n \in \{k,l\} \\
            0 & n \not \in \{k,l\}
        \end{cases}
        \; .
    \end{equation*}
    In addition, require that \(\sum_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}\beta(n)=0\).
\end{itemize}
How many shifty functions are there in $\mathcal{F}$?

Let $n \geq 6$ be a positive integer. We call a positive integer $n$-Norwegian if it has three distinct positive divisors whose sum is equal to $n$. Let $f(n)$ denote the smallest $n$-Norwegian positive integer. Let $M=3^{2025!}$ and for a non-negative integer $c$ define 
\begin{equation*}
    g(c)=\frac{1}{2025!}\left\lfloor \frac{2025! f(M+c)}{M}\right\rfloor.
\end{equation*}
In addition, $M$ is even.
We can write 
\begin{equation*}
    g(0)+g(4M)+g(1848374)+g(10162574)+g(265710644)+g(44636594)=\frac{p}{q}
\end{equation*}
where $p$ and $q$ are coprime positive integers. What is the remainder when $p+q$ is divided by $99991$?

